+    delta="minNnDist",
+    family=mgcv::scat(link = "log"),
+    sample_id="patient_id",
+    image_id="image_name", 
+    condition="patient_stage",
+    algorithm="bam"
+)
+
+names(resLs)
 ```
 
-First, we will plot the functional box plot of the square-root transformed spatial statistics functions [@Sun2011-boxplots].
+The convenience function `crossSpatialInference` calculates first the spatial statistics
+functions and then compares these with a functional additive mixed model across all cell types indicated in `selection`. [@Baddeley2015-book-point-patterns; @Baddeley2005-spatstat; @Scheipl2015-additive; @Scheipl2016-generalized; @Goldsmith2024-refund-package]. The result is a list of lists containing the results across all cell types. 
+
+We can plot the overall picture of the interactions by performing an $F$-test on all functional models and plotting both the $p$-value of the tests as well as the mean coefficient over the domain $r$.
+
+```{r, spatialFDA-bubbleplot, warning=FALSE, message=FALSE, fig.width=8, fig.height=4, results='hide'}
+p <- plotCrossHeatmap(resLs, coefficientsToPlot = c("conditionLong_duration(x)",
+                                                    "conditionOnset(x)"), 
+                      QCThreshold = 0, QCMetric = "medianMinIntensity")
+
+p <- p + guides(shape = "none") + 
+  facet_wrap(~factor(coefficient, 
+                     levels = c("conditionOnset(x)", "conditionLong_duration(x)"), 
+                     labels = c("conditionOnset(x)" = "Onset", 
+                                "conditionLong_duration(x)" = "Long-Duration")))
+
+p
+```
+
+This plot highlights an increased co-localisation of T-cell types with pancreatic $\alpha$ cells in Onset diabetes but not in Long-duration diabetes. This is an interesting overall finding and we will focus on the cell type pair $\alpha$-cytotoxic T cells in more detail below.
+
+```{r, spatialFDA-results-selection, warning=FALSE, message=FALSE, fig.width=4, fig.height=4}
